 ULTIMATE WAF-BYPASSABLE PAYLOAD COLLECTION  —  UNIFIED / DEDUPLICATED
================================================================================
SOURCE : ALL 2006 reports of `reports-tips.txt` (bug-bounty writeups) + advanced.
RULE   : For every vulnerability, the WAF-BYPASS TECHNIQUE is stated FIRST,
         then ADVANCED WAF-BYPASSABLE PAYLOADS follow. No basic/trivial
         payloads are included (plain <script>alert(1)</script> is deliberately
         omitted — only obfuscated / parser-differential / encoding variants).
USAGE  : Authorized security testing & defensive research only.

The recurring WAF-evasion PATTERNS observed across all 2006 reports (P1-P42):
  P1 ENCODING DIVERGENCE - WAF decodes differently than the sink (double URL-encode, HTML entities, UTF-7/base64 data URIs, overlong UTF-8, Unicode NFKC).
  P2 PARSER DIFFERENTIAL - WAF vs backend use different grammar (`;/` path normalize, chunked TE smuggling, Content-Type switch, HPP, boundary tricks).
  P3 WHITESPACE/COMMENT FILL - break keyword signatures with /**/ %09 %0a.
  P4 CASE / SPLIT / SPOOF - UnIoN, split tokens, backtick grouping.
  P5 OOB / SEMANTIC BYPASS - when obvious sinks are blocked, go blind/OOB or swap to request/OS globals.
  P6 PROTOCOL / ADDRESS OBFS - decimal/octal/hex/IPv6/enclosed-Unicode IPs, `@`/`#` authority tricks.
  P7 JS-URI NEWLINES - `javascript://%0aalert(1)` and `javascript://...;%2f%2f@` beat filters that block `javascript:` followed by `(`.
  P8 OPENER / TABNABBING - `window.opener.location.replace(...)` / `opener.eval()` bypass same-origin checks on postMessage/redirects.
  P9 METADATA CLOUD OBFS - GCP `metadata.google.internal` / `100.100.100.200`, EC2 `/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/...`.
  P10 INTEGER-OVERFLOW DoS - 0x7fffffff / 0x80000000 / 4294967286 sized allocations exhaust memory; distinct from ReDoS string bombs.
  P11 NESTED/POLYGLOT HTML - `<select<style/>W<xmp<script>`, broken `on onload`, attribute injection inside filenames, hashrocket `{...}`.
  P12 INFRA/PROTOCOL TRICKS - chained Content-Encoding, `curl --globoff token[]`, IPv6 zone `[ipv6%25lo]`, `view-source:`, `.git/logs`.
  P13 TERMINAL/ANSI INJECTION - backslash-e escape sequences inside BasicAuth username or log lines (terminal/tmux escape injection).
  P14 HOMOGLYPH + NULL-IN-URL - Cyrillic a (#1230), null bytes %00 (#1119), `%01` (#1155), `%0a` in username (#1422).
  P15 INTERNAL-ENDPOINT DISCLOSURE - Spring `/env /dump /trace`, Eureka PUT, Nextcloud `/WEB-INF/`, WDDX packets, Actuator.
  P16 FORMULA / CSS-EXPRESSION INJ - `=1+1` spreadsheet (#1194), IE `expression()` (#1491).
  P17 BBCode / WIKI-MARKUP XSS - `[url=...onclick=]`, `[url]javascript:[/url]`, MediaWiki `[[ /tabnabbing ]]`, emoticon `%%%[...]%%%`.
  P18 GLOB / PATH-PREFIX TRICKS - `--allow-fs-read=*.pub` reveals all (#1079), Varnish `key: ../1/cache` (#1262), DNS-SRV path prefix (#1460), `authorized_keys` traversal (#1246).
  P19 CHUNKED / RESPONSE-SPLITTING - 8190+ a chunked trailer (#1031), `<script>` after chunk data reflected in error (#1456), hex `0a0a` (#1319).
  P20 OAUTH / REDIRECT-CHAIN CONF - wrong-scope redirect (#1178), FB redirect chain (#1385/#1424), host confusion (#1330), `@` redirect (#1432).
  P21 IMAGE-PROCESSING RCE/CRASH - JPEG embedded `%!PS`/`%pipe%curl` (#1443), oversized GIF/PNG dims (#1270/#1417).
  P22 NODE/PERL/RUBY MEMORY-DoS - `$ENV{"A"x0x1000}` (#1182), 10MB password (#1389), regex DoS (#1303), Ruby crash primitives (#1232/#1481).
  P23 EMAIL / AUTH BYPASS - unicode-split `@` (#1008), empty password (#1190), OTP `0000` (#1151), `OC-Signature=notchecked` (#1057).
